course: dictionary
lesson: 11431
title: Activation: making things start working
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Activation means making something start working or become active. The word comes from the verb «activate», which means to switch something on or bring it to life. The ending -ion turns the verb into a noun, so activation is the name for the action itself.
explain: «Enter your activation code to start the game.» The sentence tells you what the code is for: it wakes up the game so you can play. Activation is the step that turns something from off to on. If you swap in «starting», the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Activation is often used with cards, accounts, alarms and software. «The bank sent an activation email after I opened my account.» The account was not working until the activation was done. Scientists use the word too: «Heat caused the activation of the yeast» means the heat made the yeast start working.
fact: Activation means making something start working or become active.
fact: «Activate» is the verb, and «activation» is the noun for the action of activating.
fact: «An activation code» is a code that switches on a product, account or program.
fact: In science, activation can mean making yeast, enzymes or the immune system start working.
fact: Activation is mostly uncountable, but «an activation» can name one single case.
exercise: «Enter your activation code to start the game.» What is an activation code for? | To change the colour of the screen | To delete the game from the computer | To make the game boring | *To turn the game on so it can be used
exercise: What does activation mean? | Painting a picture | *Making something start working or become active | Making a loud noise | Making something stop working for ever
exercise: Activation comes from which verb? | actor | actually | *activate |Activist
test: «The heat caused the activation of the yeast.» What does activation of the yeast mean here? | The yeast turned cold and still | The yeast was counted and weighed | The yeast was thrown away | *The yeast started working
test: Which sentence best shows activation? | *A sleeping phone screen lights up when you press the button | A plate falls off the table and breaks | A book is closed and put back on the shelf | A cup is filled slowly with tea
exam: In «The activation of the account took two days», what does activation mean? | *The process of making the account start working | The number of people who use the account | The closing of the account for ever | The stealing of money from the account
